# Copy to .env and edit.   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and must stay that way: AMD_PASSWORD is a shared LAN credential, and
# the only thing that keeps it out of the image and out of git is that it lives here and
# nowhere else. Nothing in this file is baked into the image at build time -- compose passes
# it to the container's environment, and the image itself has no credential in it.
#
# Generate the two secrets rather than typing them:
#   AMD_PASSWORD=$(openssl rand -base64 24)
#   AMD_SESSION_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The hub's own login password. One shared password for the whole web UI, no default, and
# load_settings refuses to start without it. It is NOT the Apple account password: Apple
# credentials are typed into the web form and reach the wrapper on the login child's argv,
# which is a deliberate exposure recorded in spec §11 and never persisted anywhere.

AMD_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recommended
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Keeps logged-in browsers logged in across `docker compose restart` and across an image
# rebuild. Optional by design: with it unset, load_settings generates a fresh 32-byte secret
# per process, because a *missing* secret must never degrade into a constant that ships in
# the image. The cost of leaving it empty is that every restart invalidates every session and
# you log in again. Must be at least 32 characters; a shorter one is rejected at startup
# rather than truncated, because a short secret makes the session cookie forgeable.
AMD_SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Library roots
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The list is the container-side mount points, comma-separated. Every entry is scanned --
# dedup matches against all of them at once, and the order does not change any answer
# (`scan_roots` builds one index across all roots, so a track in root 2 is found whichever is
# first). Order is therefore not a correctness concern.
#
# *** /library/a MUST BE IN THE LIST. *** `dirPathFormat` is baked into the image's client
# config as /library/a/{album_artist}/{album} -- upstream's own example is relative, and a
# relative value would resolve against AppleMusicDecrypt/ rather than the mount. So the client
# always writes to /library/a, and if you drop it from this list then downloads land in a tree
# nothing ever scans: every track is re-downloaded, forever, and nothing errors. Adding the
# external drive means ADDING to the list, not replacing what is in it.
#
# This is the one mistake here with no diagnostic at all, and no build can catch it, because
# this variable is read at runtime. TODO(spec §8.1, Phase 2): assert at boot that the
# dirPathFormat root is a member of AMD_LIBRARY_ROOTS and refuse to start with a message naming
# both, rather than warning after the first silent re-download. It belongs in `create_app`'s
# lifespan, next to the three startup steps, reading the root out of the vendor config the same
# way `hub/deploy/build_gate.py` does -- ten lines, and it is the last unchecked way this
# configuration can be wrong.
#
# The library is the external drive, and it is the only root. `/library/b` is the container
# path; the host side is `LIBRARY_B` below, and compose mounts it with `create_host_path: false`
# so an absent drive is a failed start rather than an empty library that reads as healthy.
#
# This value should be `/library/b` and nothing else. It is also baked into the image as the
# client's `dirPathFormat`, from the same build argument, so a `.env` that names a different
# root than the client writes into produces a silent re-download of everything. Nothing can
# check that at runtime today; it is a TODO in `hub/deploy/build_gate.py`'s own comment.
AMD_LIBRARY_ROOTS=/library/b

# There is no second root to add. The drive is either mounted, or compose refuses to
# create the host path and the container does not start.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional overrides
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment to widen or narrow the published port on the HOST side. The container always
# listens on 8080; only the left-hand number changes.
# AMD_HTTP_PORT=8080

# Region metadata language, written into <vendor>/config.toml at build time. Change it here
# and run `docker compose up -d --build` again.
# AMD_VENDOR_LANGUAGE=ja

# Dedup artist matching. `loose` (the default) treats two same-named albums as one album,
# which is what catches a collaboration fanned out across every credited artist's folder --
# 164 of the 223 real duplicate album names in this library. `strict` additionally requires
# the artist to match, which removes the false-skip mode at the cost of those 164. Either
# way `skip_reason` names every path that matched, so a human can overrule a bad call.
# See spec §7.4.
# AMD_DEDUP_ARTIST_SCOPE=loose

# How many tracks to rip at once. The default of 4 is measured, not guessed: a 41.8 MB ALAC
# track takes 9.8 s here, and 6.1 s of that is the wrapper answering /lyrics, the album
# lookup and the codec check before a byte of audio moves. The audio then crosses at ~41 MB/s
# in about a second, so roughly 85% of a track's wall clock is an API round-trip -- which a
# serial queue spent waiting for a sibling that was not running. Four overlapping rips
# recovers most of that, and it is a number to put on a home connection without worrying the
# Apple account. Upstream's own ceiling (`maxRunningTasks`, 128) is tuned for a TUI driven by
# a person and is not a number to send from a LAN box.
#
# Raise it for a bulk backfill of many short tracks; lower it to 2 if Apple ever complains.
# `1` restores the original one-track-at-a-time queue, which is also the honest way to
# measure what the concurrency bought. Zero or less is refused at startup rather than
# quietly claiming work it never started.
# AMD_RIP_CONCURRENCY=4

# The host-side paths behind the two library mounts. You should not need to touch these: the
# defaults are this machine's. They are here because a bind mount's source is a host path and
# a relative one is resolved against the directory compose runs in.
# LIBRARY_B=/home/m/Music/HDD_Music
